        "reason": "Carrier A (request with GET): idempotent, read-only, should never mutate data on server. Carrier B (request with POST): NOT idempotent, creates new resource, may cause duplicate creation on retry. Carrier C (request with custom method): semantic depends on method — PUT is idempotent update, DELETE is idempotent delete, PATCH is non-idempotent update. Unifying these would create an HTTP client method where the SAME code path (curl_setopt_array) could produce either idempotent or non-idempotent behavior depending on the method string. This is DANGEROUS because callers cannot reason about retry safety."
